    "slug": "unbound-flesh",
    "title": "Unbound Flesh",
    "link": null,
    "metaLines": [
      "soft cover",
      "170*260 mm",
      "316 pages",
      "digital print"
    ],
    "creditsBefore": [],
    "description": [
      "Many people around me have gone back to eating meat. I often think about the way people let go of their worldviews relatively suddenly. I searched for words to explain this phenomenon, and what's happening here in our country more broadly — the sense that we keep walking toward some infinite point, not knowing when we'll stumble.\nHow can one prepare for a fall?\nOr at least, how can it be softened?",
      "In a time when violence has become routine, and the separation between the private and the political, between body and spirit, is collapsing — eating has stopped being an innocent act. This book examines how empathy is shaped in times of war and crisis, through the culture of meat in this time and place."
    ],
    "creditsAfter": [
      {
        "text": "Graduation project, Guided by Meirav Solomon and Dan Ozeri"
      }
    ],
